Quoting  Jove  <invalid@invalid.invalid>:
>On 8 Feb 2006 11:44:00 -0800, "sjdevnull@yahoo.com"
>>The problem here is that simple damage just isn't a deterrent to people
>>who want to power up forever.  
>A better question is why people want to power up forever.
>And so what if people power up forever?  It won't save them
>from instadeaths, so it's just one more resistance to another 
>form of death.

Then we can approach the problem that all late-game deaths are
instadeaths, not least by making some of them not instadeaths.

One of the strengths of Crawl (this rant pp Martin Read) is that almost no
attack results in an instadeath. Hence there is no non-negotiable
resistance; you can always survive with enough HP and tactics to avoid
being hit repeatedly.

But we can't get that as long as players can accumulate an infinite number
of HP.

The other difficulty at the moment is every late-game monster is either a
nightmare or a blot on the windshield. Almost nothing is a moderate amount
of trouble.

>>Eliminate Elbereth in Gehennom--the lady can't help you here.
>Elbereth in Gehennom is like having four-wheel drive in a 
>swamp:  It just means you'll be in *real* trouble when it's
>no longer enough.  

Well, no. Sure, you can get into trouble by assuming it's a panacea, but
put yourself next to Demogorgon and ask if you'd rather have E on the
ground or not?

>>Yes.  Also forbid wishing for Quest artifacts.
>A healer could have the +7 Mitre of Holiness, the Eye of 
>Aethopica, a robe, and one thousand mana points, and the healer
>still couldn't advance spell skills in any school except healing.

Well, they'd only have the Eye and the Mitre with a very careful alignment 
shuffle, but they'd still (at high level) be able to cast level 5 spells
at 0% failure and make utility use of level 6 and 7 spells; they would
still receive the enormous boost to mana regenration.

>  Any non-Valkyrie could have gauntlets of power and Mjollnir, 
>but Mjollnir still wouldn't return to their hand when thrown.

On the other hand a non-Valkyrie with the Orb of Fate receives all the
benefits, and aren't we talking Quest artifacts?

Worse still, a Quest artifact granting magic resistance is _more use_ to
someone who is not of that Quest artifact's class.

